r a server you control. It covers three things: starting the two stacks, watching every turn on the dashboard, and how the two websites ship to Azure.\n\nOn your machine, the coding agent\u0027s stack serves its API on port 5082. The other stack runs louis-agent.dev on port 5080 and this site on 5084. Every port binds only to your own machine.\n\nThe Aspire dashboard shows each turn, model request and tool call as a trace, with its logs. It runs on port 18888, and it keeps everything in memory, so a restart clears it.\n\nIn Azure, every merge to main releases both sites through \u0060deploy-sites.yml\u0060. Each site is one Container App that sleeps when nobody visits. The first visitor after a quiet spell waits a few seconds.\n\nsrc/docs/projects/LouisAgent.Web.Framework.md"},{"$type":"functionCall","name":"Offer","arguments":{"question":"Where would you like to go next?","choices":[{"label":"Walk me through this page","why":"One section at a time, in the page\u0027s order.","suggested":true},{"label":"Start the coding stack","why":"The commands and every setting it needs."},{"label":"What is the Aspire dashboard?","why":"How it shows every turn as a trace."}]},"informationalOnly":false,"callId":"toolu_015DL9dHbGttsbkM5dpxfo2a"}],"messageId":"msg_011ChSvXMH4Quo6nt7YvmrmB"}],"responseId":"msg_011ChSvXMH4Quo6nt7YvmrmB","modelId":"claude-haiku-5-5","createdAt":"2026-11-27T06:01:05.4482985\u002B00:00","finishReason":"tool_calls","usage":{"inputTokenCount":10118,"outputTokenCount":1070,"totalTokenCount":11188,"cachedInputTokenCount":9217,"additionalCounts":{"CacheCreationInputTokens":897}}}